  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.1-preview.27\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.27 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.26\n- Documents the Android permission requirement. The readme now states that UseMaui() registers AndroidNetworkDetector, which queries ConnectivityManager and therefore needs ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE in the consumer's AndroidManifest.xml. Both ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE and INTERNET are install-time permissions that never prompt at runtime, and omitting ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE fails silently rather than throwing.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.25\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.25 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.24\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.24 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.23\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.23 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.22\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.22 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.21\n- Made framework-free: removed Microsoft.Maui.Controls, UseMaui, and the dead MauiNetworkDetector internal. UseMaui() now delegates to the native platform packages only.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.20\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.20 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.19\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.19 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.18\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.18 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.17\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.17 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.16\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.16 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.15\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.15 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.14\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.14 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.13\n- Updated to depend on FireForNet.Firebase.Firestore 1.0.1-preview.13, which adds offline-first optimistic writes (opt-in via FirestoreBuilder.OptimisticWrites) and eliminates the proto-to-JSON round-trip on typed model conversion. Offline writes persist via the SQLite backend.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.12\n- Updated to depend on FireForNet.Firebase.Firestore 1.0.1-preview.12, which fixes ObjectDisposedException on SemaphoreSlim.Release() during network disable and UnobservedTaskException from WebChannel receive-loop exceptions during concurrent disposal.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.11\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.11 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.10\n- Updated to depend on FireForNet.Firebase.Firestore 1.0.1-preview.10, which fixes the \"Cursor has too many values\" error on snapshot-cursor pagination queries.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.9\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.9 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.8\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.8 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.7\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.7 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.6\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.6 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.5\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.5 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.4\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.4 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.3\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.3 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.2\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.2 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.1\n- Synchronized package version with the preview10 release.\n\nv1.0.0-preview9\n- Synchronized package version with the preview9 release.\n\nv1.0.0-preview8\n- Picks up the Firestore SQLite RemoveIndexAsync rename and the shared public field-index encoder.\n\nv1.0.0-preview7\n- Adopted plan-based QueryCandidatesAsync local-cache contract with broad-scan fallback.\n\nv1.0.0-preview6\n- Synchronized package version with the preview6 Firestore cache-query release.\n\nv1.0.0-preview5\n- Synchronized package version with the preview5 release.\n\nv1.0.0-preview4\n- Synchronized package version with the preview4 release.\n\nv1.0.0-preview3\n- Synchronized package version with the preview3 release.\n\nv1.0.0-preview2\n- Initial v1.0.0-preview2 package.",
